      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I've upvoted this but also want to share some information that might explain why this isn't a thing (anymore?)\nThis comment on Proton issue tracker makes a nice summary of video issues on linux so far:   https://github.com/ValveSoftware/Proton/issues/1199#issuecomment-1214202488\nThere are over 600 comments on the linked issue but it is surely an information gold mine.  \nUsing the comment linked above I discovered I was missing the i386 vdpau-drivers, as the 64bit versions don't seem to be used. After adding those I can report (partially) working video players on Linux. (Ubuntu 22.04, 5.17-oem kernel)\nI have not tested streams but comments lead me to believe they still don't work. It also does not work in Proton 7.0_4, but is currently working in Proton Experimental.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
